**Search and rejection summary**
I checked the official statistics and implementation trail rather than adding more macro-only repeats. I retained 2022 household-income, distribution, social-security, rent-support, and recovery-disbursement sources because they directly address the gap. I did not add additional GDP/CPI/FDI-only pages because those are already covered in the existing evidence index and do not materially improve household-level or implementation-specific coverage. A direct open of two NSO pages timed out, so I used their search snippets instead. A few broader background items, including retrospective World Bank/ILO material, were considered but not needed because the official 2022 series now does the gap-closing work more directly.

**Remaining gaps**
Partly resolved. What is still thin is direct province-level audit data, household microdata, and tighter causal attribution from Trọng to the observed household and distribution outcomes rather than to the PM, ministries, provincial authorities, and external shocks. More search would help if you want to push this from partly resolved to fully documented, especially on provincial execution quality and bottom-quintile or ethnic-minority outcomes in 2022.
